{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ErBmRBZ11LDiUganEPCMuV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tNo prior `length-budget.md` exists in any book repo, so this is the first instance of the retired-word-budget format. Emitting to stdout for the orchestrator to capture.\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t```markdown\n6\t# Question Budget — KCNA\n7\t\n8\t**Book:** Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate\n9\t**Exam:** KCNA (CNCF / The Linux Foundation), curriculum effective 2025-11-24\n10\t**Stage:** B4 — Question Budget\n11\t**Date:** 2026-08-23\n12\t**Input:** Stage B2 chapter lineup (20 chapters — 1 orientation, 17 content, 1 synthesis, 1 mock)\n13\t\n14\t> **Word-count budgets were retired 2026-04-24** (style-decisions.md § \"Length Budgets\").\n15\t> This file produces no word targets. Chapters and sections are whatever length the\n16\t> material requires. The filename is retained for pipeline compatibility only.\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Per-chapter question budget\n21\t\n22\tPer skill v5.3 Part 8 \"Practice-Question Budget\":\n23\t\n24\t- **Floor: 300 questions per book.**\n25\t- **Mock Exam** (final chapter): matches real exam size (or performance-task count for performance-based exams)\n26\t- **Soundings**: 8 per content chapter; 5 per orientation/synthesis; 0 per mock_exam\n27\t- **Taking Your Bearings**: minimum 10 per content chapter (across ≥2 checkpoints)\n28\t- **Practice Questions** (end-of-chapter): `(300 − mock_exam − soundings_total − bearings_total) × domain_weight_pct / 100`\n29\t\n30\t### The formula returns a negative pool for this book — see § \"Practice-question derivation\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3bc0fa3e-307a-47e7-ad10-30a96a63cfe3","uuid":"53e95233-a6bc-444d-803c-87374976560d","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:24:48.956Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\length-budget.md","content":"No prior `length-budget.md` exists in any book repo, so this is the first instance of the retired-word-budget format. Emitting to stdout for the orchestrator to capture.\n\n---\n\n```markdown\n# Question Budget — KCNA\n\n**Book:** Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate\n**Exam:** KCNA (CNCF / The Linux Foundation), curriculum effective 2025-11-24\n**Stage:** B4 — Question Budget\n**Date:** 2026-08-23\n**Input:** Stage B2 chapter lineup (20 chapters — 1 orientation, 17 content, 1 synthesis, 1 mock)\n\n> **Word-count budgets were retired 2026-04-24** (style-decisions.md § \"Length Budgets\").\n> This file produces no word targets. Chapters and sections are whatever length the\n> material requires. The filename is retained for pipeline compatibility only.\n\n---\n\n## Per-chapter question budget\n\nPer skill v5.3 Part 8 \"Practice-Question Budget\":\n\n- **Floor: 300 questions per book.**\n- **Mock Exam** (final chapter): matches real exam size (or performance-task count for performance-based exams)\n- **Soundings**: 8 per content chapter; 5 per orientation/synthesis; 0 per mock_exam\n- **Taking Your Bearings**: minimum 10 per content chapter (across ≥2 checkpoints)\n- **Practice Questions** (end-of-chapter): `(300 − mock_exam − soundings_total − bearings_total) × domain_weight_pct / 100`\n\n### The formula returns a negative pool for this book — see § \"Practice-question derivation\"","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":233}}}
